From 400aac5d258796a22c233e914ec21500699a4c83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 15:12:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: Release the PHY init when the link is not powered

The DP PHY init is shared with the USB side of the QMP combo PHY. While
DP holds it, qmp_combo_usb_init() skips the common block init, and after
a system suspend that lost power the USB PHY times out waiting for
PHYSTATUS.

Two paths keep the init after the sink is gone:

- An enable that fails link training takes the init in
  msm_dp_display_prepare_link() but leaves power_on false, so
  msm_dp_display_disable() returns before releasing it.
- An unplug while the display is off releases it only when sink_count
  is 0, and a USB-C unplug does not change sink_count.

Release the init in both cases. Only drop the PHY init: after a failed
training the link is already down and its registers must not be
touched.

Signed-off-by: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
index fc3f97aa84..b2795abbd6 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -504,7 +504,7 @@ static int msm_dp_hpd_unplug_handle(struct msm_dp_display_private *dp)
 		drm_edid_connector_update(dp->msm_dp_display.connector, NULL);
 
 	/* triggered by irq_hdp with sink_count = 0 */
-	if (dp->link->sink_count == 0)
+	if (dp->link->sink_count == 0 || !dp->msm_dp_display.power_on)
 		msm_dp_display_host_phy_exit(dp);
 
 	/*
@@ -753,8 +753,10 @@ static int msm_dp_display_disable(struct msm_dp_display_private *dp,
 {
 	struct msm_dp *msm_dp_display = &dp->msm_dp_display;
 
-	if (!msm_dp_display->power_on)
+	if (!msm_dp_display->power_on) {
+		msm_dp_display_host_phy_exit(dp);
 		return 0;
+	}
 
 	msm_dp_panel_disable_vsc_sdp(msm_dp_panel);
 
